        "pageTitle": "Stefanie Posavec",
        "pageDescription": "I",
        "evidenceText": "Stefanie Posavec 0 Hello! I’m Stefanie, and I help people use data to communicate, educate, and bring communities together. ‍ ‍ As a creative director, artist, and author I enjoy extending the boundaries of data and information communication, turning both into memorable, participatory ‘information experiences’ that spark conversations and help build deeper understanding and connections. From art installations to agency collaborations, I create data-driven work that is intuitive, human-scaled and accessible, celebrating the humanity found within every dataset.  As a creative consultant, I work with R&D teams, design agencies, and corporate clients, leading creative direction and early-stage concept ideation for data-driven products of the future, or by creating data-driven artwork for campaigns. Sometimes I work as a 'cartographer of the unknown', mapping complex systems, emerging ideas, or messy, unstructured data to help stakeholders start conversations, make sense of systems, or support change. I also design low-tech, participatory tools that help communities document lived experience, bringing visibility to their voices in non-extractive, restorative ways. My recent work designing the text and art-directing the charts for Greta Thunberg’s The Climate Book . Photo copyright: Penguin Random House / Greta Thunberg I also speak about data, design, and creativity at conferences and corporate events, inspiring audiences to see data differently and explore more human-centred approaches to data communication. Additionally, I lead hands-on workshops that use basic drawing materials to build participants’ confidence in designing custom data visualisations. By focusing on core design principles over tech tools, these workshops are accessible and transformative for all skill levels – from newcomers to seasoned data professionals. I’ve led workshops for leading organisations across tech, education, government, and design, helping teams move beyond basic charts to develop creative, impactful data visualisations. Discover my range of workshops My work has been featured at major galleries worldwide including MoMA , the Storefront for Art and Architecture (New York), the Centre Pompidou (Paris), ArtScience Museum (Singapore), V&A (both South Kensington and Storehouse), the London Design Museum (‘ Designs of the Year 2016 ’), the Wellcome Collection , the Science Museum , The Southbank Centre, and Somerset House (London), Bletchley Park , and is also in the permanent collection of MoMA. Gallery view of Dear Data project during MoMA’s Search Engines exhibition within their permanent galleries (Room 209). Photo credit: Walter Wlodarczyk I’m also the co-author (with Miriam Quick ) of the award-winning book, I am a book. I am a portal to the universe. , an illustrated book visualising wondrous data from the universe on a 1:1 scale. It was named one of the Financial Times’ Best Books of 2020 and winner of the Royal Society’s Young People’s Book Prize 2021 . Learn about my other books Interested in collaborating? Get in touch",
