        "pageDescription": "The global OpenStreetMap conference. 2026 in Paris & online.",
        "evidenceText": "State of the Map 2026 × Paris State of the Map 2026 State of the Map is the annual event for all mappers and OpenStreetMap users. In 2026 the State of the Map conference took place in Paris and online. It was a three day conference packed with talks, workshops, discussion rounds and more. Thank you for attending! In case you missed a particular talk or want to re-watch a particular one, you can find recording of all talks on Peertube (and linked from the conference Programme here). Also, take a look at this year's conference Posters . And don't forget: It's never too late to connect with other attendees on our chat rooms on Matrix or Telegram , or on our social media channels, e.g. Mastodon . Your organising team. State of the Map 2027 We're excited to announce that SotM 2027 will be hosted in Bogotá, Colombia! Below are a few words as an early invitation from the local team in Colombia: “Dear OpenStreetMap community: greetings from Colombia! We are thrilled and honored to welcome State of the Map 2027 to Bogotá. After many years, the global conference returns to Latin America, and our community could not be more excited to host you. The conference will take place in July 2027 at the campus of the National University of Colombia, a green, historic campus in the heart of the city — the same venue where we recently celebrated State of the Map Colombia. Behind this bid is the whole Colombian OSM community, led by AC3, our local chapter, together with mappers from across Latin America who have long dreamed of bringing SotM to the region. Bogotá awaits you at 2,600 meters closer to the stars, with eternal spring weather, coffee, music, and the warmth of our people. ¡Nos vemos en Bogotá!” Where? Paris, France Cité Descartes, Champs-sur-Marne 48° 50′ 30″ N, 2° 35′ 15″ E When? August 28 - 30, 2026 Partners   Support OpenStreetMap! OpenStreetMap is free to use, but not free to run. If you wish to further support the project, head over to OpenStreetMap's donation page to find out how you can help improve its stability, quality and independence. Our Sponsors Platinum “Every year, State of the Map brings together individuals and organizations that are pushing the boundaries of what open mapping can achieve. It is a unique space where local knowledge meets global impact, and where ideas evolve into collaborations that benefit the entire OpenStreetMap ecosystem. TomTom is proud to support an event that continues to strengthen the OSM ecosystem and foster meaningful collaboration across the mapping community. We look forward to the conversations, innovations, and partnerships that will emerge from this year's State of the Map, helping to drive the future of open mapping forward.” “Michelin is building a world-leading manufacturer of life-changing composites and experiences. Pioneering engineered materials for more than 130 years, Michelin is uniquely positioned to make decisive contributions to human progress and to a more sustainable world. Drawing on its deep know-how in polymer composites, Michelin is constantly innovating to manufacture high-quality tires and components for critical applications in demanding fields as varied as mobility, construction, aeronautics, low-carbon energies, and healthcare. The care placed in its products and deep customer knowledge inspire Michelin to offer the finest experiences. This spans from providing data- and AI-based connected solutions for professional fleets to recommending outstanding restaurants and hotels curated by the MICHELIN Guide. Headquartered in Clermont-Ferrand, France, Michelin is present in 175 countries and employs 122,600 people.” Gold Silver Bronze Supporter FerryGoGo YellowMap OpenRunner Neogeo Infrageomatics Association du Réseau des Urfist krick.com MITFAHR|DE|ZENTRALE",
