        "evidenceText": "BARC Start-Up Award | Analytics und Datenmanagement Skip to content BARC Start-up Award for Data & AI 2026 R ecognizing innovative software solutions that generate business value from data. SOLISTIQ wins the BARC Start-up Award 2026. The Würzburg-based start-up builds an autonomous Inventory Planning Agent that automates stock decisions with a proprietary AI foundation model. The aim is to cut excess inventory, prevent supply shortages, and make planning much more efficient across retail, e-commerce, and supply chain management. Background Start-ups are a significant source of innovation in the software market for analytics, business intelligence, data management, and artificial intelligence . They introduce new approaches and solutions to address long-standing industry challenges. To honor their contributions, BARC established the annual Start-up Award for Data & AI . The award honors software product providers for data & AI. Service providers are not eligible to apply. Eligibility Requirements To qualify, a company must meet the following criteria: The business must have been operating for six years or less. This six-year rule also applies to spin-offs and new business units within established companies, such as a new standard software offering from an existing consulting firm. The company must be headquartered in Germany, Austria, or Switzerland , or maintain an office in the DACH region. The solution must be a software product or a software-supported service in the field of analytics and AI, business intelligence, planning and simulation, or data management. The product must exist at a minimum as a functional, demonstrable prototype. Get Your Start-up the Visibility and Recognition it Deserves Participants in the BARC Start-up Award for Data & AI get significant visibility among decision-makers across data, analytics, and start-up ecosystems. Finalists selected by the jury will present their solutions to enterprise users, established vendors, and investors at the DATA festival in Munich. The presentations will be available to both the live audience and virtual attendees via streaming. The Jury The jury members includes market analysts, investors, and end users : Prof. Dr. Peter J. Mirski, Head of Department & Studies & CIO | MCI The Enterpreneurial School Jörg Bienert, President & Founder | KI Bundesverband e.V. Wolfgang Beeck, CTO | Staedean Group Dominik Lohle, Founding Partner | MAY VENTURES Stefan Sexl, Senior Analyst Data & AI | BARC GmbH Holger Wagner, Investment Manager | EnBW New Ventures Christian Wirth, SVP APAC | IQGeo Simone Nierhaus, Chief Commercial Officer | Flyeralarm Arthur Michael Seidel, Senior Corporate Community Manager | Fraport Markus Roithmeier, Partner Zobito AB & Business Angel | IACD e.V. Dr. Thomas Endres, CEO | corporate momentum Frank Hoelzle, CEO | Care4 AG Prof Dr. Frauke Schleer-van Gellecom, Partner & Professor for Decision Intelligence | PWC Tobias Stein, Chief Venturing Officer | AI Hub Frankfurt Sören Dreis, Investment Manager | HTFG Chairman : Dr. Carsten Bange, Founder & CEO | BARC GmbH Previous winners of the BARC Start-up Award 2025 encentive 2024 Scavenger AI 2023 Frontnow 2022 Veezoo 2020 4.screen 2019 minubo 2018 Open as App 2017 Process Analytics Factory 2016 Inspirient Any questions? Contact us! Email [email protected] Email [email protected] Contact If you have any questions about the Start-up Award, please contact event manager Christina Schuhmann. Phone +49 931 880 65 10 DATA festival Munich. Experience Data & AI with the community shaping what’s next. Join us on March 17 – 18 Privacy Preference We need your consent before you can continue on our website. If you are under 16 and wish to give consent to optional services, you must ask your legal guardians for permission. We use cookies and other technologies on our website. Some of them are essential, while others help us to improve this website and your experience. Personal data may be processed (e.g