        "pageTitle": "AGI Awards 2026 - AGI",
        "pageDescription": "The AGI provides fantastic opportunities to exhibit at our national events throughout the year with several sponsorship packages.",
        "evidenceText": "AGI Awards 2026 - AGI Skip to content AGI Awards The AGI celebrating excellence in the geospatial Sector AGI Awards 2026 Showcasing innovation, achievement, and best practice, the AGI Awards celebrate excellence in geospatial and are open to any individual, group or organisation that can demonstrate and communicate success through the use of geographic data, knowledge or technology. “We have once again been inspired, and even humbled, by the quantity, quality, diversity, and impact of the submissions and nominations received for this year’s awards,” commented Fergus Craig, Chair of the Association for Geographic Information. “We are delighted to showcase so many exceptional talents and innovative projects and we look forward to working with the award winners to share these examples of geospatial excellence with a wider audience.” AGI Awards 2026 Showcasing innovation, achievement, and best practice, the AGI Awards celebrate excellence in geospatial and are open to any individual, group or organisation that can demonstrate and communicate success through the use of geographic data, knowledge or technology. With the exception of the Chris Holcroft Award, all awards will require a submission, and entries will be judged by an independent panel of thought leaders and geospatial experts from academia, commerce, and professional organisations. The AGI will present its Awards for Excellence at the UK’s largest geospatial event GEO Business. Working with event organisers Diversified Communications, the Association will also have a significant presence on the show floor, which it will use to make announcements about new AGI Networks, forthcoming surveys and research activities, and outreach events. Award submissions has now closed, any queries please feel free to contact our AGI Member Support on info@agi.org.uk AGI Awards Categories Chris Holcroft Award We are presenting this award in honour of the late Chris Holcroft. Chris was known to many in the geospatial community, notably through his work and leadership of the Association for Geographic Information 2007-2012 when he was instrumental in allowing AGI members’ voices to be heard by government and industry. This award celebrates recognition and contribution to the UK Geospatial Industry. Award Winner – Denise McKenzie In honour of the former Chief Executive of the AGI, the Chris Holcroft Award was presented to Denise McKenzie, Managing Partner at the PLACE Trust. In the words of AGI Chair Fergus Craig, ‘ this award recognises an exceptional and sustained contribution to the geospatial profession, demonstrated through more than 25 years of international leadership and advocacy’ . He added, ‘through her ability to connect communities, influence global thinking, and embed ethical principles into practice, Denise has made a lasting, and meaningful impact on the profession, making her a highly deserving recipient of this award’ . As this award acknowledges Chris’s legacy and his own contributions to the Association and wider industry, it is fitting that Denise is also a former Chair of the AGI. AGI GeoCommunity Champion 2026 Bruce Gittings , Senior Lecturer in Geographic Information at the University of Edinburgh, and Chair of AGI Scotland. This award recognises Bruce’s ability to bring people together, champion talent and strengthen the geospatial ecosystem. Submit your entry AGI Award Geospatial Professional of the Year 2026 Dr Andy Brewer , Development Manager at Idox Geospatial for his work on Natural England’s award-winning Green Infrastructure Map Submit your entry AGI Award Early Career Professional of the Year 2026 Gabriella Edghill , Geospatial Analyst at Rebalance Earth, who received the Early Career Professional of the Year Award for her work on a Geospatial Predictive Analytics Platform (GPAP), advancing climate risk methodology and making the case for nature-based investment. Submit your entry AGI Foresight Award 2026 The Crown Estate for the Marine Delivery Routemap initiative. Aligned with the highly acclaimed AGI Foresight Report 2030, and the themes and calls for outcomes contained within, this award looks at future partnerships between government, industry and regulators. It was described by the judges as ‘an impressive foresight approach to model seabed use to 2050 for long-term impact. Submit your entry AGI Environment & Sustainability 2026 Arcadis SuDS Project team. Applying advanced geospatial workflows to analyse London’s streetscape and rank over five million potential drainage opportunities, it is hoped this will support the delivery of greener, more climate-resilient urban environments Submit your entry AGI Award for Innovation in Geospatial Technology 2026 Sizewell C SDP GIS Team at AtkinsRéalis . Turning complex nuclear design into accessible 3D information, this project will transform how 3D engineering data is accessed, validated, and shared, so that it is accessible to all. Submit your entry AGI Submission Terms and Conditions AGI Awards Categories Chris Holcroft Award We are presenting this award in honour of the late Chris Holcroft. Chris was known to many in the geospatial community, notably through his work and leadership of the Association for Geographic Information 2007-2012 when he was instrumental in allowing AGI members’ voices to be heard by government and industry. This award celebrates recognition and contribution to the UK Geospatial Industry. We will not be accepting submissions for this award, this will be chosen and awarded by AGI Chair Fergus Craig. AGI Award Geospatial Professional of the Year 2026 This award is open for professionals who have demonstrated and communicated success through the use of geographic data, knowledge or technology. Submit your entry AGI Award Early Career Professional of the Year 2026 This award is open for nominations of professionals within the first 10 years of their geospatial career. Submit your entry AGI Foresight Award 2026 This award is open to submissions from projects that relate to one of the six Foresight Themes: Data in the world of Geospatial Artificial Intelligence in Geospatial Interoperability and Infrastructure The Great Skills Shift Collaboration in Geospatial Earth Systems Evolution Submit your entry AGI Award for Environment and Sustainability 2026 The award for Environment and Sustainability celebrates geospatial projects, applications and products that contribute to the sustainability of people to co-exist on our planet. This could be impacting a small change in a local area or tackling one of the larger issues facing our world today. Submit your entry AGI Award for Innovation in Geospatial Technology 2026 This award recognises ground-breaking advancements in geospatial technology, whether through new processes, software, hardware, data collection methods, or innovative applications of AI, automation, or big data. It celebrates forward-thinking solutions that push the boundaries of what is possible in the industry. Submit your entry AGI Submission Terms and Conditions AGI Award Ceremony Join us when we announce the AGI Award winners at GEO Business 2026, Wednesday 3 June from 16:00. GEO Business is a two-day event which takes place at the ExCel London on the 3-4 June 2026 Attracting over 6,000 professionals who will discover and debate the latest technical advancements and best practice in the geospatial sector, GEO Business features an exhibition of over 110 leading brands and start-ups and an education programme made up of 150 plus sessions, across 7 theatres, covering new trends, informative case studies and pressing industry issues. Further Information and Register your place AGI Award Geospatial Professional of the Year 2026 This award is open for professionals who have demonstrated and communicated success through the use of geographic data, knowledge or technology. Submit your entry AGI Award Early Career Professional of the Year 2026 This award is open for nominations of professionals within the first 10 years of their geospatial career. Submit your entry Copyright © 2015-2026 AGI. All rights reserved | Privacy Policy | Website Terms and Conditions | Membership Terms and Conditions | Code of Conduct We use cookies on our website to give you the most relevant experience by remembering your preferences and repeat visits. By clicking “Accept”, you consent to the use of ALL the cookies. Cookie settings ACCEPT Manage consent Close Privacy Overview This website uses cookies to improve your experience while you navigate through the website. Out of these, the cookies that are categorized as necessary are stored on your browser as they are essential for the working of basic functionalities of the website. We also use third-party cookies that help us analyze and understand how you use this website. These cookies will be stored in your browser only with your consent. You also have the option to opt-out of these cookies. But opting out of some of these cookies may affect your browsing experience. Necessary Necessary Always Enabled Necessary cookies are absolutely essential for the website to function properly. These cookies ensure basic functionalities and security features of the website, anonymously. Cookie Duration Description cookielawinfo-checbox-analytics 11 months This cookie is set by GDPR Cookie Consent plugin. The cookie is used to store the user consent for the cookies in the category \"Analytics\". cookielawinfo-checbox-functional 11 months The cookie is set by GDPR cookie consent to record the user consent for the cookies in the category \"Functional\". cookielawinfo-checbox-others 11 months This cookie is set by GDPR Cookie Consent plugin. The cookie is used to store the user consent for the cookies in the category \"Other. cookielawinfo-checkbox-necessary 11 months This cookie is set by GDPR Cookie Consent plugin. The cookies is used to store the user consent for the cookies in the category \"Necessary\". cookielawinfo-checkbox-performanc