        "pageTitle": "The Pudding Cup",
        "pageDescription": "The Pudding",
        "evidenceText": "The Pudding Cup Skip to main content The Pudding Cup The best visual and data-driven stories of 2026 To be completely honest: we almost didn’t do it this year. Over the last year, we’ve felt the same AI fatigue a lot of you probably have. Our inboxes and feeds have been flooded. The Pudding has always been about more than just a shiny end result. It’s about what it took to get there: the ambition, the struggle, the triumph, and the hope of sharing a discovery. We’re not here to police how you create a visual data-driven story, but if your project doesn’t have a heartbeat, it’s not getting the Cup! So, the submissions are open… for now. But if we find ourselves drowning in slop, we’ll close the form, and figure out how to reinvent the Cup into something entirely different that maintains our values. We really hope we don't have to. Here’s what you need to know: Entries are free , just give us a URL! (One per person, please) Must be your own work Must have been published / put on the internet in 2026 Highly encouraged to share your process and raw materials Up to three winners will each receive $1,500 . Deadline - Monday, November 30, 2026 Winners Announced - The week of December 07, 2026 More info in the form, but hit us up at sup@pudding.cool with questions! Submit *Non-commercial projects = things created without compensation. It was made for learning, fun, school, a contest, etc. Not for work or hire. See past winners from 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 2017 The 2025 winners Dithering — Part I By: Damar Aji Pramudita Not everything needs to be an interactive visual story. This piece, though, is an example of leveraging this medium to explain something more clearly (and more delightfully) than you could otherwise. The animations are super sleek, but more importantly, they make you say “oh, that makes sense.” Can’t wait for parts 2 and 3! —Michelle Pera-McGhee The Legislative Network Behind State Trans Laws By: C.J. Robinson It's incredibly difficult to pull off a data story where your main visuals are text, but through animations and small multiples this piece delivers. A minimal document-based design hammers home the obsurdity that trans peoples' bodies and lives are being legislated with copy/paste. —Jan Diehm Benford’s Law By: Schubert de Abreu I've come across this topic before so I was excited to read it. What made it stand out was how thorough it felt. It kept answering the questions I had, provided tons of examples, and use simple yet effective visuals. —Russell Samora Honorable 2025 mentions Who Opens the Door for Whom? By: Sihang Sun This is how the Premier League works By: SportsBall (Riley and Claire Martin) Baby Name Trends By: Karim Douieb Dogs with Jobs By: Stephanie Wu Hidden Constellations By: Yuki Zhang Grocery Signery By: Monsicha Srisuantang The Disappearing Act By: Ricardo Fernandes Garcia, Khadijah Olufayo & Jocelyn Shek This Modern Career By: Aki Matsushima",
