        "evidenceText": "Conference - Online News Association Skip to content ONA Annual Conference The Online News Association Conference, along with the Online Journalism Awards luncheon, has become the premier gathering of highly engaged digital journalists who are shaping the future of media. Each year, journalists, technologists, news executives, educators, students and more travel to ONA&rsquo;s conference each year to learn about new tools, techniques and technologies, to discuss advancements and challenges in the industry, take advantage of the rare opportunity to network face-to-face, and share best practices with peers from all over the map. They also come to soak up the vibrant entrepreneurial spirit that distinguishes ONA conferences.   ONA26 will take place March 30 &ndash; April 1, 2026 in Chicago. Subscribe to  our conference newsletter  for updates. ONA25  took place Sept. 10-13, 2025 in New Orleans. Check out the  program and speakers  from last year. ONA24 took place Sept. 18-21, 2024 in Atlanta and marked ONA&rsquo;s 25th anniversary year. Check out the program and speakers from last year. ONA23 took place Aug. 23-26, 2023, in Philadelphia and virtually from Sept. 28-29. View resources from the conference on our resources page . ONA22 offered programming for attendees joining in person in Los Angeles and online. View resources from the conference. Explore a selection of the ONA21 video archive, and learn how ONA&rsquo;s second virtual-only conference came together. Explore a selection of the video archive from ONA&rsquo;s first virtual-only annual event. Explore resources from ONA19 , including video, audio and social highlights. Explore resources from ONA18 , including video, audio and social highlights. &times; Membership & Account Access Not a Member? Create a Free ONA Account Set up your free account to sign up for events and update your community profile. Once logged in, you can: Update Your Profile Register for Events Create an Account Ready