        "pageDescription": "We work with leading media to deliver deeply reported, public interest journalism on migration, conflict and corruption. We do this by building newsrooms around topics and channeling editors, tools and resources to working journalists with the results reaching the public on existing platforms.",
        "evidenceText": "Lighthouse Reports - Pioneering Collaborative Journalism Silence Over Syria’s Stolen Children SOS Children’s Villages was used by the Assad regime to hide children and extort their parents. Years on, the troubled global charity has failed to release an investigation into its role or compensate Syrian families. Published with Investigations 30.09.2026 Chokepoints: Suffocating the West Bank How we quantified and mapped the full impact of Israel’s invisible and accelerating web of checkpoints on the 3.5mn Palestinians forcibly trapped within it. Published with 30.09.2026 Data Centre Silence How EU leaders sided with Big Tech over the public’s right to know about the true scale and environmental impact of the AI build-out, forcing a legal challenge to seek disclosure Published with 25.09.2026 Smells Like Cash For Access Leaked documents show Tony Blair Institute charges unlisted companies $25,000 to join network with active role in policy programmes as it hosts record number of serving UK ministers at ruling party conference Published with 21.08.2026 Making Southern Lebanon Unlivable Exposing how Israeli forces have systematically destroyed homes, schools, roads, healthcare facilities, farmland and forests in occupied southern Lebanon. Published with 30.07.2026 Congo’s Hidden Uranium Exports How a leaked memo prompted scientists and reporters to investigate the supply of cobalt from mines in the DRC to China, revealing the departure of strategic quantities of uranium Published with 22.07.2026 Big Food vs. The People We expose Big Food’s 239 lawsuits against life-saving policies Published with Explore Investigations Methodologies 30.09.2026 How we measured the impact of movement restrictions in the West Bank 30.09.2026 Why we made a legal filing to the Aarhus Convention Compliance Committee 21.07.2026 How we measured consolidation in France’s cattle industry from the farmer’s perspective 18.06.2026 How we analysed AI used to guess asylum seekers’ ages Explore Methodologies Backlight Podcast: Backlight 30.10.2026 Journalism Q&A episode; pitching stories, career advice, fellowships, funding & more You sent the questions. We answer them. Podcast: Backlight 25.09.2026 Do you need to go to journalism school? Part 2 (Teacher Edition) Last month we asked two early career journalists how they got in the field. This month we take the conversation to the other side of the classroom. Podcast: Backlight 28.08.2026 Do you need to go to journalism school? Does Journalism school still matter? Podcast: Backlight 21.07.2026 Reclaiming the migration narrative When migration is talked about in the language of fear and crisis, how do journalists tell the true human story? Podcast: Backlight 15.06.2026 Lessons from Local News From the UK to India and the Brazilian Amazon, we spoke with journalists who are making it work. Podcast: Backlight 06.05.2026 How can the media win back our trust? Trust in traditional media is in crisis. This is what media leaders are doing about it. Explore Backlight Work with us Lighthouse offers the opportunity to work on a fascinating range of investigations in partnership with some of the biggest media brands in Europe. We are committed to a diverse and inclusive working environment and encourage applications from under-represented groups. Job Openings",
