      "audit": {
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T20:02:55.377Z",
        "httpStatus": 200,
        "finalUrl": "https://www.tableau.com/community/iron-viz",
        "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
        "pageTitle": "Iron Viz | Win or learn-you can’t lose | Tableau",
        "pageDescription": "Where will the next great data viz come from?",
        "evidenceText": "Iron Viz | Win or learn-you can’t lose | Tableau Skip to content Register for TC26 Packing for Mars by Ann Pregler Explore Nutrition, Energy Sources, and Ingredients of Dim Sum by Kevin Wee Explore The Confection Connection by Brian Moore Explore Find your 'why.' It’s not just about winning or comparing your viz to others. Build something you love, challenge your skills, and try something new. There are countless reasons to enter—and the community has your back. You won’t regret it. CJ Mayes Tableau Visionary and Iron Viz Finalist, London, UK From Empire To Identity by Robert Taylor Explore Late-night Snacks by Shreya Arya Explore Sunday Dinners by Kimly Scott Explore Visit the gallery Design Visual elements add to the overall understanding of the visualization rather than distract Interactivity and layout are user-friendly, instructed/specified, and purposeful Charts are clearly presenting the data Charts contain a title, summary, and/or caption All charts contribute to the story Accessibility is applied - colorblind/low vision (contrast) friendly palette, limited use of images to convey text, font size 12pt or larger Analysis Viz topic aligns with contest theme Dataset and calculations appear to be accurate and clean Analysis illustrates profound insights grasped from visualizations Analysis supports the story being told Analysis has been mostly produced within Tableau Analysis highlights a broad range of Tableau capabilities Storytelling A clear story is being told Story flows through visualizations and guides consumers from question to insight Visualizations and animations support the story being told The story includes a unique idea or perspective The story being told has complexity/nuance that elevates the visualizations. Storytelling captures and maintains interest throughout the entire viz What is Iron Viz? Iron Viz is the world’s largest data visualization competition. Taking place at Tableau Conference in San Diego, three worthy contestants take center stage in front of a global audience and have 20 minutes to deliver a compelling and awe-inspiring story using the same data set. When does Iron Viz take place? Iron Viz, the world's largest data visualization competition, is held on the keynote stage at Tableau Conference every year. The three finalists are selected from a global qualifier competition, which usually happens towards the second half of the year and is open for one month. How will the winner be chosen? A panel comprised of Tableau ambassadors, previous Iron Viz finalists, data viz experts, and guest judges will evaluate all submissions based on the following criteria: Design Storytelling Analysis Analysis will be the tiebreaker in case two vizzes have the same overall score. Should the Analysis score also be tied, the panel of judges will make a final decision. Will I receive my scores or feedback if I participated in the Qualifiers? Scores and feedback can be provided upon request by filling out this form after the contest is over. How is Iron Viz: Student Edition different from Iron Viz? Iron Viz: Student Edition is a competition open exclusively to students, though we encourage you to participate in both. Iron Viz: Student Edition is intended for college students looking to develop their viz skills in a challenging setting with their peers before jumping into the greater vizzing community with Iron Viz. This competition is a great introduction into the world of viz competitions. Iron Viz: Student Edition winners will have the opportunity to connect with members of the Tableau Community with a funded trip to Tableau Conference. Visit the website to learn more and stay updated on the student competition. Try Tableau for free Buy Tableau now",
