        "finalUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/data-visualization-society-geospatial-group",
        "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
        "pageTitle": "DVS Geospatial Group | LinkedIn",
        "pageDescription": "DVS Geospatial Group | 1,504 followers on LinkedIn. To create a space where data viz practitioners interested in the geospatial data field can connect and collaborate. | To create a space where data viz practitioners interested in the geospatial data field can connect and collaborate.",
        "evidenceText": "DVS Geospatial Group | LinkedIn Agree & Join LinkedIn By clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement , Privacy Policy , and Cookie Policy . Sign in to see who you already know at DVS Geospatial Group Email or phone Password Show Forgot password? Sign in Sign in with Email or New to LinkedIn? Join now By clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement , Privacy Policy , and Cookie Policy . Skip to main content DVS Geospatial Group Data Infrastructure and Analytics To create a space where data viz practitioners interested in the geospatial data field can connect and collaborate. Follow Report this product About us To create a space where data viz practitioners interested in the geospatial data field can connect and collaborate. Website https://www.datavisualizationsociety.org/dvs-geospatial External link for DVS Geospatial Group Industry Data Infrastructure and Analytics Company size 2-10 employees Updates DVS Geospatial Group reposted this Shira Ellenson, GISP 5h Edited Report this post #30DayMapChallenge | Day 10: Prompting Only I feel mixed about this one. I asked Claude to make a James Niehues-inspired oblique render of Alyeska Resort. I used a smoothed Alaska IfSAR DEM and had it generate real contours, then added OpenStreetMap lifts, ski trails, and land cover. Sarah Bell’s High Alpine font and an edge fade for the final touches. It took about 20 prompts over an hour (mostly rendering and placing 10,000 trees), with 1/3 of that spent on fine-tuning the last 10%. I wonder a few things - Does this look obviously AI? Does the use case depend on if this is \"cheating\"? Where's the line drawn? Is \"real\" cartography dying? Here's the final proof, along with a few prompts in progress. #alyeska #jamesniehues #AImapping #claude 37 3 Comments Like Comment Share DVS Geospatial Group reposted this José Marín Fariña 4h Edited Report this post Day 10 of the #30daymapchallenge , theme: prompting only. I just tried something new: I asked Claude (Opus 5.5) to build an entire map directly in Blender using Blender MCP (never used it before) and SciAtlas, the geospatial extension I'm developing (not public yet). No coding on my side, just a prompt. I basically told it to use everything SciAtlas has to offer to visualize the 2026 US elections, with terrain, county-level results, and animations sorting counties by size, state and votes. I gave it two of my previous maps as visual references and let it do its thing. And well... in about an hour, it had found the data, downloaded everything and built the renders! Of course, it wasn't perfect. I had to point out missing states, ask for a separate color for independents, make decisions about using AP's data, and fix some design choices. It still lacks a bit of an eye for design, especially when it comes to labels and composition. Interestingly, Claude caught some of its own mistakes by rendering frames and inspecting them. It also helped me discover ways to improve SciAtlas. For example, it exposed how inefficiently the SciAtlas compositor was baking EXR images for Blender's compositor, which was taking much longer than necessary. So I ended up getting a usability test out of it too. My favourite is the last render. Republicans won 1,914 counties versus 510 for Democrats, yet Democratic candidates received 39.8 million votes compared to 33.5 million for Republicans. When counties are resized according to their votes, the huge sparsely populated areas shrink and the cities grow. How was it made according to Claude (only using operators): - Terrain: GEBCO and Copernicus GLO-30, loaded through SciAtlas. - Counties: US Census 1:500k shapefiles, imported and projected onto the terrain with SciAtlas. - Results: A GeoTIFF generated by Claude and draped over the relief. - Camera and labels: SciAtlas Geo Camera and compositor. The results are still unofficial, with some states still counting. Everything is scripted, so I can rerun it once the final results are certified. Far from fully autonomous, and Claude still needs some design lessons... But seeing it build all this in about an hour in real time, while also helping me find ways to improve SciAtlas, was pretty amazing. #Blender #SciAtlas #MCP #Elections2026 #GIS #OpenData #DataVisualization #30daymapchallenge 10 1 Comment Like Comment Share DVS Geospatial Group reposted this John Nelson 1w Report this post Experimenting with stacked flow renders in ArcGIS Pro today. Here's six months of wind, which looks like a tangle of silk. I'll share the how-to on Monday. …more 109 3 Comments Like Comment Share DVS Geospatial Group reposted this Geoawesome 21,169 followers 2w Report this post Geospatial teams in different countries often face similar challenges: updating land records, sharing data across agencies and turning new technology into reliable services. That makes international exchange valuable. At GISTC International in Haikou, Michalis Kalogiannakis , Vice President of FIG - International Federation of Surveyors , joined a program that brought together more than 120 experts, industry leaders and researchers from 15 countries, according to the organizers. Participants shared experience from national projects and discussed how GeoAI and geospatial data infrastructure can support their work. FIG’s support and Michalis’s participation were part of the event’s international character. We look at what made the first edition useful, and why GISTC deserves attention as you plan your 2027 conference calendar. Dates for the next edition remain to be confirmed. Read the article on Geoawesome: https://lnkd.in/dAUwP8QQ #GISTC #Geospatial #Surveying #FIG SuperMap GIS View C2PA information 9 Like Comment Share DVS Geospatial Group reposted this James Tan Song En 6h Report this post Day 10 of #30DayMapChallenge Prompting Only For this one I handed the wheel to Claude Opus 5.5 and asked it to make a map of New York City in the style of Stardew Valley. The pixel aesthetic was something I wanted to try for a while but could never quite get right myself. The rules I set included 1) no AI image generated map, 2) every pixel had to come from real geographic data and code and 3) it had to find the data and show me the code it used. It handled the whole workflow from start to finish from downloading the open data (streets, subway lines, surrounding counties) to processing and projecting everything in Python and creating the pixel textures (grass tufts, water sparkle, little trees in the parks) in code. My job was mostly reviewing checking colour contrast, making sure the labels were legible and verifying accuracy. I checked the landmarks and didn’t spot any major issues. It was genuinely impressive to read back through the whole pipeline. It’s not perfect and still needed a human eye, but it’s a big leap from the AI-only map I made two years ago. #GIS #Cartography #AI #Python #PixelArt #StardewValley #NYC 34 2 Comments Like Comment Share DVS Geospatial Group reposted this Andrew James 14h Edited Report this post #30DayMapChallenge , Day 9: Urban-Rural Quick one. Used WorldPop Hub for a geotiff of population density across the US by kms to show how quickly things change from urban to rural population densities along lines. Uses a d3 linear scale & exaggerated values to be more visible. Lines are every 0.25' of latitude. Data Source: WorldPop Color theme: `piccadilly-sparrows` by avilluk on ColorLovers 24 2 Comments Like Comment Share DVS Geospatial Group reposted this John Nelson 3w Report this post I had a blast co-hosting the CMPASS iron cartographer competition with Kate Berg, and brave competitors Alex Biles and Emmett Smrcka . Coordinated by Mariah Modson. Good times had by many! 193 9 Comments Like Comment Share DVS Geospatial Group reposted this Lindsey Peña, MBA, MPhil, PhD 2d Report this post #30DayMapChallenge Day 8: Utopia. A world full of animals, trees, colorful landmarks, and possibilities, all waiting to spark a little imagination. I couldn't think of a better map to depict \"Utopia\" than this! This #MapsInTheWild find is in the kid's room at the Pandell, an ESG Company office in Houston, TX. And that Pandell offers such an inviting space for kids? I'm tempted to move in for a while. Think they'd notice? 🤭 💙 💛 🩷 #30DayMapChallenge #Lindseys30DayMapChallenge2026 #Utopia #Geospatial #GIS #Cartography #MapsInTheWild 62 Like Comment Share DVS Geospatial Group reposted this Ryan DeLine 5h Edited Report this post What does field work look like for catographic marine map production? Come join our Map Chats with Experts next week Thursday for the Data Visualization Society Geospatial Group's expert guest, Courtney Edwards , and learn about life on the water in field work and cartography. *DVS Plus Members get an exclusive backstage stage pass to join Courtney after her talk. When: November 19th, 12pm EST | 17:00 UTC Register here: https://lnkd.in/gZyQi-Ff #DVSGeoIG #DataViz #MarineCartography #GIS #Mapping #SeaLife 12 Like Comment Share DVS Geospatial Group reposted this Sandon Lettieri 4d Report this post #30DayMapChallenge - Day 6 - Vintage For today’s map, I fired up my old Dell Inspiron 600m from my college days (2005 to 2008) as a beginner GIS student. I originally wanted to get the ArcGIS 9.x installation running but that license had long expired (no surprise). I did happen to install QGIS 1.6 on that machine well over a decade ago so I thought it might be fun to try and make a map using that. Glad I bumped the RAM up to 2GB back then, that Pentium M was getting a workout. Below is a window into that time capsule. 38 3 Comments Like Comment Share Join now to see what you are missing Find people you know at DVS Geospatial Group Browse recommended jobs for you View all updates, news, and articles Join now Affiliated pages Data Visualization Society Professional Training and Coaching Washington, District of Columbia Similar pages storytelling with data Business