        "evidenceText": "Data Art Technology | Domestic Data Streamers Fighting indifference towards data We are a research and design studio partnering up with organisations to build change through data, community, and arts. What we do Upcoming Events Date Name Location Country 15 Mar 2026 - 13 Dec 2026 Barcelona Complexa - Capitalitat Arquitectura Exhibition Edifici Gustavo Gili Barcelona - Spain Exhibition Edifici Gustavo Gili Barcelona - Spain An exhibition on the architecture and urban space of the city 15 Mar 2026 - 13 Dec 2026 Barcelona Complexa - Capitalitat Arquitectura Exhibition Edifici Gustavo Gili Barcelona - Spain Exhibition Edifici Gustavo Gili Barcelona - Spain An exhibition on the architecture and urban space of the city 17 Sep 2026 - 17 Jan 2027 Uncoded Gestures Exhibition Galeria Mayoral Barcelona - Spain 17 Sep 2026 - 17 Jan 2027 Uncoded Gestures Exhibition Galeria Mayoral Barcelona - Spain Exhibition Galeria Mayoral Barcelona - Spain Uncoded Gestures 27 Sep 2026 - 13 Jun 2027 Full Disclosure: The Edge of Information Design Exhibition Museum of Modern Art - MoMA New York - US Exhibition Museum of Modern Art - MoMA New York - US The Museum of Modern Art announces a new exhibition, Full Disclosure: The Edge of Information Design, MoMA’s first devoted entirely to information design. On view in the Museum’s street-level gallery—which is free and accessible to the public— from September 27, 2026, through June 13, 2027, Full Disclosure will feature 30 works of digital and analog information design, including six newly acquired works. This exhibition will explore the many ways in which humans visualize information and how designers, operating in an increasingly complex digital world, can facilitate and shape our understanding. The show will also seek to recognize the fundamental role of information design, a medium that has evolved into a defining practice of the 20th and 21st centuries and a pillar of the Museum’s design collection. More info 27 Sep 20