on OL Owen Lin 6 1.4M Stock Levels Published Inventory Copilot I track stock across your distribution centers and can post reorder lists to Slack. Access to Inventory Slack What runs out in Dallas this week? Queried Inventory as you: Central region only 3 SKUs run out before Friday's delivery. Sparkling Water 12oz is shortest, with 2 days of cover. Post the reorder list to #dallas-dc ? Approve Skip Ask a follow-up Security that follows the user Queries run with the viewer’s own warehouse permissions, down to the row. Set access once, and dashboards, AI answers, and agents follow it. Visibility into everything built Audit logs record who built, changed, and asked what, including AI conversations, so IT always knows what’s running. Control what you spend Sigma reuses cached results instead of querying your warehouse again, and usage dashboards show which workbooks and people drive the load. SOC 2 Type II PCI DSS HIPAA GDPR SSO & SCIM Visit the Security Center Finance Sales Marketing Operations Supply chain Sigma Slack Claude Codex ChatGPT Terminal Order Fulfillment Published Orders at risk $1.2M Shipping this week Short-ship orders 9 Of 212 this week Actions logged 9 of 9 By Fulfillment Agent Fulfillment Actions 9 rows written by Fulfillment Agent Retailer Order Issue Plant Action 1 Northgate Grocers $214K Line 4 down 9 hrs Monterrey Ship from Reno DC 2 Fresh Basket $188K Short 1,200 cases Monterrey Split ship, rest Fri 3 Summit Outdoor $156K Line 4 down 9 hrs Monterrey Move run to Line 2 4 Bayview Pharmacy $131K Resin delivery late Toledo Expedite resin PO 5 Cornerstone Market $118K Short 640 cases Toledo Ship from Reno DC 6 Pine & Co. $97K Labels on hold Toledo Confirm with buyer order-fulfillment Sigma APP Mon 6:00 AM Fulfillment Agent : Line 4 at Monterrey was down 9 hours overnight. 3 retail orders could now ship short (Northgate Grocers, Fresh Basket, Summit Outdoor). Actions are in Fulfillment Actions. Open Order Fulfillment in Sigma Fulfillment Agent Which retail orders could ship short this week? Found 2 data sources 9 orders worth $1.2M could ship short. Most trace to 9 hours of downtime on Line 4 at the Monterrey plant. Orders Line Events Reroute what you can and log the rest Write to Fulfillment Actions 9 rows · Plant, Action Northgate Grocers Ship from Reno DC Fresh Basket Split ship, rest Fri Approved by you Done. Planners have an action logged for each order. Ask a follow-up Answers the questions that used to wait in a queue Agents answer everyday data questions in plain language from your governed warehouse, so analysts stop fielding the same requests week after week. Watches the numbers so no one has to Agents run on a schedule, catch what changed overnight, and send a summary with next steps before anyone opens a dashboard. Takes the next step for you When an answer calls for action, agents write back to your warehouse, log the next step, and notify the right team, with your approval and the permissions you already have. Everything an app needs already in place Instant, secure deployment Security and hosting you never have to prompt for Month-end close Publish SO PS JE AK ML Live Finance team · 42 people SSO and row-level security No servers to stand up or logins to generate. Apps go live under the SSO, teams, and permissions you already have. Warehouse-native Always on the latest data and context Your warehouse Live Writeback Input tables Forms and actions Workflows Embedding Your product Apps query your warehouse live, write data back, and run workflows with forms and actions. Connect and control Connect your data and AI, and see what it costs AI tokens 413M 34% Plug in your warehouse and AI models. Admins see the agents people build and the tokens each one uses. Enterprise governance Everything is always secure Viewing as Priya , EMEA Row-level security On Column-level security On Audit log On Row-level and column-level security follow each user. Audit logs record changes and AI conversations. Customers build their businesses on Sigma How teams build analytics, applications, and agents on Sigma. View all “ Using Sigma, I was able to make a dashboard in under two hours that got the answers. The AI features let our team move faster than ever before. ” 91% active user adoption How Duolingo Democratized Data Access While Protecting Sensitive Information “ Sigma eliminates the boundary between data entry and data consumption. We are moving a lot faster than we were before. ” How Conagra Uses Sigma to Build Smarter CPG Workflows and Empower Brand Teams “ Since Sigma, we’re able to have a lot more trust in our metrics. Now we know when people go into Sigma, the data is up to date. People know what they're doing, they understand the data. ” How Sigma and HashiCorp drove record BI adoption Recent highlights View all blog posts November 10, 2026 Turn complex scheduling into a Sigma App with self-service optimization Sigma · 1 PM ET / 10 AM PT November 10, 2026 Workbooks and Reports as Code are now GA: Build Sigma assets from any agent Akshay Devalla + 2 · 13 min read November 3, 2026 Sigma Tables are now in public beta Gic Gad · 9 min read October 30, 2026 New in Sigma October 2026: dashboards you describe and spreadsheets that go live Luke Stanke · 5 min read Self-service analytics Ask Sigma Assistant or explore in a spreadsheet, on live data Dashboards Interactive views any team can filter and drill into Reports Pixel-perfect reports that stay on live data Applications AI Apps that write back and take action Embedded Analytics and apps inside your own product Data models Define metrics once and reuse them everywhere Agents Agents that run your workflows, in chat or on their own Writeback Input Tables that save edits to your warehouse CLI, MCP, and plugins Build from Claude, Codex, ChatGPT, or the terminal Sales ops Published Straight from the source “ Sigma brilliantly blends the familiar simplicity of a spreadsheet with the immense power of cloud data warehouses… ” Frederik Gillis Data Analyst · Enterprise · G2 (opens in a new tab) “ …its write-back capabilities enable users to build interactive data applications rather than just dashboards. ” Director of Data and Analytics Healthcare and Biotech · Gartner Peer Insights (opens in a new tab) “ Sigma’s AI assistant has become a complete game-changer for ad-hoc requests. ” Cherry Lin Principal Data Analytics, GTM · Enterprise · G2 (opens in a new tab) “ Sigma queries directly against the warehouse, so users are always working with current data, not stale CSVs. ” Director of Finance Finance · Gartner Peer Insights (opens in a new tab) “ We like that it’s not just a BI platform, it’s more of a workflow platform. ” Andrew Dennis Director of Data · Mid-Market · G2 (opens in a new tab) “ I love the ability to interact with and create metrics with our data without making core changes to the governed and centralized data warehouse. ” Product Analyst Software · Gartner Peer Insights (opens in a new tab) “ …my data is directly linked which means there’s no need for refreshing, and there’s absolutely no lag. ” Elizabeth Wang Enterprise · G2 (opens in a new tab) “ Reports are now live, actions can be taken immediately, and collaborating with colleagues is faster and more accurate than it has ever been. ” Alex Burcum Sr. Data Analyst · Small Business · G2 (opens in a new tab) Get started Ask me anything about your data Free trial self.__next_f.push([1,\"73:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",\\\"recent-highlights\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"data-sanity\\\":\\\"id=homepage;type=recentHighlightsSection;path=pageBuilder:8;base=https%3A%2F%2Fsigma-website.sanity.studio\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",\\\"recent-highlights\\\",{\\\"id\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"relative isolate overflow-hidden bg-white pb-20 pt-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L81\\\",null,{\\\"bands\\\":\\\"$6d:props:children:props:children:0:props:bands\\\",\\\"s