        "evidenceText": "dbt Developer Hub Skip to main content Relive the best of dbt Summit! Get access to the keynotes and breakout sessions from dbt Summit 2026. See the latest product innovations from dbt, and hear how data teams are leveling up for the agentic era. Quickstart New to dbt? Start here. Guide Get started with dbt Get up and running quickly with our dbt quickstart guides. Article About dbt Explore dbt and discover how its shared Rust runtime delivers faster, more scalable performance. Guide Move to the dbt platform Move from self-hosted dbt to the dbt platform and follow recommended best practices for building scalable data pipelines. Documentation by product Explore the docs by product dbt Wizard AI agent purpose-built for analytics engineering — available in the dbt platform and from your terminal. VS Code Extension This free tool brings the full power of the dbt into your local environment with features like live error detection, lightning-fast parse times, insights and rich lineage all in VS Code or Cursor. dbt State dbt State makes dbt smarter about what to build — skipping unnecessary rebuilds by reusing nodes when logic and data haven't changed. Works with self-hosted dbt and the dbt platform. dbt Orchestrator Every time a job runs, state-aware orchestration automatically determines which models to build by detecting changes in code or data. dbt Insights dbt Insights in dbt empowers users to seamlessly explore and query data with an intuitive, context-rich interface. dbt Semantic Layer The dbt Semantic Layer eliminates duplicate coding by allowing data teams to define metrics on top of existing models and automatically handling data joins. dbt Catalog Use dbt Catalog to navigate and manage your projects within dbt to help you and other data developers, analysts, and consumers discover and leverage your dbt resources. Studio IDE The dbt integrated development environment (Studio IDE) is a single web-based interface for building, testing, running, and version-controlling dbt projects. dbt Mesh dbt Mesh is a framework that helps organizations scale their teams and data assets effectively. Docs highlights Dive deeper into dbt Learn best practices, explore detailed configuration references, or review our APIs. Documentation API Docs Product Docs Best Practices dbt Wizard Guides Quickstart for dbt and Snowflake Quickstart for dbt and Databricks Airflow and dbt Debugging errors Reference Guides Command Reference Project Configurations dbt Artifacts Other Resources Release Notes Developer Blog Join the Community Get help from others Join the dbt Community Connect with thousands of developers solving real data problems every day. Join Slack Ask questions, get answers, and meet people who speak your data language. GitHub Discussions Join technical threads or open issues. Subscribe to the newsletter Get fresh community ideas, job posts, and tools delivered weekly. Answer a question on Discourse Help someone solve a real problem—and build your reputation doing it. Webinars Upcoming and on-demand sessions from dbt Labs. Events Meetups, conferences, and community gatherings. Courses & Tutorials Learn dbt with hands-on guidance. From the team Read the developer blog Deep dives, changelogs, best practices, and new feature highlights from dbt Labs. Have dbt skills been bitter lesson’d? Models have improved a lot since we shipped dbt agent skills, so I ran Claude Opus, Sonnet, and Haiku 5.5, and then Sonnet 4.5, through a... ai Read more Inside the dbt Wizard harness: building an agent that thinks in DAGs Wizard works like an analytics engineer: it thinks in DAGs, tests and fixes its own work, and keeps you in flow, so you review a working... ai Read more dbt_context_engineering: modeling the context your AI agents read dbt-context-engineering is a new package, published by dbt, that helps you create AI ready data when you need it. ai context engineering data ecosystem Read more",
