gether we have created resources that are now widely used by funders, policymakers, and practitioners working in this space. Dina Khaskelberg Program manager, JX Fund Why us Consulting discipline, built under constraint Our founding team trained at McKinsey and INSEAD — and ran newsrooms through revolutions, war and exile. That combination is the method: Western consulting rigor, plus the Eastern European habit of transforming under pressure, with small budgets and no stable ground. It's also why we work where most consultancies won't. Independent media in difficult markets is supposedly a sector without money. The 50+ organizations we've worked with — and results like Hromadske's near-4× revenue growth — suggest otherwise: the economics can work, if someone does the work. Clients & partners We bring solutions to make life easier for our customers. Request full pitchdeck Clients & partners We bring solutions to make life easier for our customers. Request full pitchdeck Let's work on your transformation Get in touch via form or email us - partnerships@thefix.media Click to copy email address Full Name * Looks good! Please enter your name. Email * Looks good! Please provide a valid email address. Your organization Looks good! Please enter your organization. Message * Looks good! Please enter your messsage. * These fields are required. LinkedIn · Email × At the Anne-Marie and Gustaf Ander Centre for Media Studies at SSE Riga, our mission is to secure a sustainable future for independent journalism through education, specialized training, and cross-border collaboration. We know that sustainable media businesses are vital for maintaining independent journalism and public accountability. Our collaboration with The Fix Team has been one of the pillars in delivering on this mission, allowing us to merge academic rigour with practical, modern industry insights. Together, we have collaborated closely on our Future Media Management projects - ranging from our four-week Mini-MB