        "evidenceText": "United Nations DPoA MTR Journalism Fellowship 2027 (Fully-funded) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram United Nations DPoA MTR Journalism Fellowship 2027 (Fully-funded) Jude Ogar October 27, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: November 30, 2026 Applications are open for the United Nations DPoA MTR Journalism Fellowship 2027 . This is a fully funded opportunity for journalists from Least Developed Countries to attend and cover the 2027 Midterm Review of the Doha Programme of Action (DPoA MTR) in Doha, Qatar. The DPoA is the overarching framework for accelerating sustainable development and supporting sustainable graduation from the LDC category. The High-level Midterm Review is an opportunity to take stock of implementation, assess progress and gaps, and strengthen partnerships for the remainder of the decade. Priority Areas Reporting proposals are encouraged to engage with one or more of the six DPoA priority areas. Investing in people: Eradicating poverty, improving health, education, and social protection, and building human capital so that no one is left behind. Leveraging science, technology and innovation: Using these tools to address multidimensional vulnerabilities, close the digital divide, and accelerate progress toward the SDGs. Supporting structural transformation: Diversifying and modernizing economies to create sustainable, inclusive growth and reduce dependency on volatile sectors. Enhancing international trade and regional integration: Expanding LDCs’ access to global markets, strengthening regional cooperation, and improving trade facilitation. Addressing climate change, environmental degradation and resilience: Combating climate risks, restoring ecosystems, recovering from COVID-19 impacts, and building adaptability to future shocks. Mobilizing international solidarity and partnerships: Strengthening global cooperation, innovative financing, and support mechanisms to achieve sustainable graduation. Benefits Selected Fellows will receive: Round-trip economy-class travel to Doha, Qatar Daily subsistence allowance for accommodation and meals, in accordance with applicable United Nations rules Participation in pre-conference orientation activities, where applicable Access to Fellowship briefings and networking opportunities Eligibility Applicant must be aged 18 years or older and a national of one of the 44 Least Developed Countries. Work regularly published or broadcast by a recognized media outlet — staff or freelance. At least two years of professional journalism experience. Willing and able to travel to Doha for the duration of the Midterm Review and to participate in all required briefings and programme activities. Application Click here to apply For more information, visit DPoA MTR Journalism Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article CODESRIA Research Grants on University Ecosystems 2027 Next Article Data for Health Leadership Lab (D4HLL) 2026 Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
