        "evidenceText": "Knight-Wallace Fellowship (International Applicants) - GFMD « Back to all Fundings Knight-Wallace Fellowship (International Applicants) Organisation: Wallace House Center for Journalists Status: Open Type: Fellowship Theme: Media support Deadline: 01/12/2026 Eligibility: International (non-U.S. citizens) mid-career journalists Target Region: International (non-U.S. citizens) Application Language: Not Specified The Knight-Wallace Journalism Fellowships offer an academic year of study, collaborative learning and access to the resources of the University of Michigan for selected journalists to pursue ambitious journalism projects. Eligibility Qualified applicants must have a minimum of five years of experience and be currently working in some aspect of journalism for a news organization or as an independent journalist. The programme is looking for a diverse range of journalists, including reporters, editors, data experts, visual journalists, audio producers, engagement specialists, designers, developers, entrepreneurs and organizational change agents. If you are not a full-time journalist, the majority of your work should be in journalism. The programme does not consider public relations writers, internal trade writers, lobbyists, public advocates, or those seeking a degree. If you are not a U.S. citizen, apply as an international applicant, even if you work in the United States or for an American journalism entity. A Green Card is not the same as citizenship. How to Apply Fill out and submit the application form by 01 December 2026. International applications uploaded under the U.S. application portal will not be considered. Review the guidance for preparing your international application and the application FAQs before submitting. Apply here . For more information, please visit this page . For the latest funding opportunities, profiles of media donors, and expert insight from GFMD’s MediaDev Fundraising Guide sign up for Bottom Line newslette