        "evidenceText": "Yale World Affairs Fellowship – Grants for Journalists Skip to content View Full List Grant details View all grants Yale World Affairs Fellowship The Maurice R. Greenberg World Fellows Program is a four-month, full-time residential program based out of Yale’s International Leadership Center and housed within the Jackson School of Global Affairs . The Program runs annually from mid-August to mid-December. The Program provides World Fellows the opportunity to expand their vision, learn from each other, and grow personally and professionally. World Fellows contribute to Yale’s intellectual life, give talks and participate on panels, collaborate with peers, audit classes, and mentor students. It is NOT open to U.S. residents. Location All Locations (Open to Anyone) Funding Type Fellowship Organization Yale University School of Global Affairs Focus Area Subject Area Varies Award Size Fellows receive fully funded compensation package designed to support fellows while they are in residence at Yale Career Stage Applicants should be between five and 25 years into their professional careers, with demonstrated and significant accomplishments at a regional, national, or international level. The average age of a World Fellow is 39, though there is no minimum or maximum age limit. Editor's Note Highly competitive. They receive thousands of applications from around the globe for an extremely limited number of fellowships. Deadline 12/02/2026 Apply Here",
