        "pageDescription": "",
        "evidenceText": "Tarbell AI Fellowship – Grants for Journalists Skip to content View Full List Grant details View all grants Tarbell AI Fellowship The Tarbell Fellowship is a one-year program for journalists interested in covering artificial intelligence. Fellows secure a 9-month placement at a major newsroom; prior to placements, fellows complete a three-month program on AI and journalism fundamentals . This remote program requires a full-time commitment and includes a custom curriculum, guest lectures, and graded assignments. It culminates in the weeklong in-person summit, an intensive week of guest speakers, workshops and networking events. Travel and accommodation costs are fully covered. The fellowship runs from June 2027 to May 2028. Fellows who excel in their newsroom placements are eligible for an additional one-year extension, through May 2029. Location All Locations (Open to Anyone) Funding Type Fellowship Organization The Tarbell Center for AI Journalism Focus Area Subject Area Artificial Intelligence Award Size $75,000 to $120,000 for early-career fellows; $115,000 to $135,000 for senior fellows Career Stage Early career; senior fellows Editor's Note Deadline 11/22/2026 Apply Here",
