        "evidenceText": "WAAW Foundation Scholarship 2027 for Female College Students in Africa – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram WAAW Foundation Scholarship 2027 for Female College Students in Africa Jude Ogar November 2, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: Unspecified Applications are open for the WAAW Foundation Scholarship 2027 . WAAW Foundation Scholarship enables female college students in Africa to pursue their studies in a STEM-related course. With this scholarship, you are free to focus on achieving your academic goal and volunteer to give back to your community and promote the engagement of women in STEM through the STEM Outreach Chapter at their university. They are looking for scholars that show a need, have the passion, and drive to make a difference in their community. Scholarship The WAAW Foundation scholarship is a one-time award of $500. Eligibility Open to female students of African origin, living and studying in Africa. Currently enrolled in a Bachelor’s degree program. Studying STEM-related courses in a University or college in Africa. Presently a first or second year student or a third-year student for a 5-year course in a University. Ability to demonstrate financial need Excellent Academic Record. Proven leadership, volunteering, and community service Below the age of 32 years. Application Applications will require the following: 2 Reference Letters 1 scanned copy of your school ID card. Signed and sealed copy of your current university transcript. (Required during the Second Stage Review) Click here to apply For more information, visit WAAW Foundation Scholarship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Planet Health Film Fund 2027 (£20,000 award) Next Article EEP Africa Rising Energy Leader 2026 Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 November 10, 2026 Closes in 24 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. 