oral and postdoctoral researchers, providing financial support of EUR 800 per month. Eligibility Applicants must be researchers affiliated with a university outside Austria and must not have been employed by the University of Vienna at any time in the last six months. Applicants must propose a research project that aligns with one or more of the Faculty of Law’s research priorities. In addition, a letter of endorsement from a university professor, a member of staff with a habilitation, an associate professor or an assistant professor at the Faculty of Law is required. This should include a brief explanation of why the applicant is particularly well-suited for the fellowship. Application A complete application must include the following documents: A completed application form . A letter of application (maximum three pages) outlining the proposed research project, its alignment with the faculty’s research priorities and the academic expertise of the proposed supervisor, as well as the applicant’s motivation for choosing the Faculty of Law at the University of Vienna as their host institution. A curriculum vitae (CV) (maximum three pages) including the five key publications for senior fellows and postdoctoral researchers; for predoctoral researchers a letter of recommendation from their supervisor. PhD students are additionally required to submit a letter of recommendation from their current supervisor at their home university. A supervision agreement from the Faculty of Law at the University of Vienna. Applications may be submitted to [email protected] from 1 November 2026 to 30 November 2026 (inclusive). Selection decisions will be made in December 2026. For more information, visit University of Vienna Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article 21 Hot Job Opportunities Currently Open – November 5, 2026 Next Article How to Ace Your Scholarship Interview: 12 Tips to Help You Stand Out Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is 