        "evidenceText": "Global Changemakers’ Media Impact Academy 2027 for Youth in the USA (A chance to win a $1,000 grant) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Global Changemakers’ Media Impact Academy 2027 for Youth in the USA (A chance to win a $1,000 grant) Opportunity Desk November 6, 2026 3 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: December 18, 2026 Applications are open for the Media Impact Academy , a Nationwide initiative engaging 500 youth across the United States. Designed for young adults navigating early financial independence, this 90-day challenge equips you with practical financial skills, project management tools, and storytelling capabilities to transform your personal habits and drive real community impact. Whether you are managing money on your own for the first time, or looking to lead change in your community, this program provides real-world tools and direct monetary rewards as you learn. In partnership with Wells Fargo and Univision, Global Changemakers is hosting a nationwide program designed to empower young adults ( ages 18–24 ) in the U.S.A through media training, storytelling, leadership development, and financial literacy. It is only open to youth in the US. This 90-day challenge equips participants navigating early financial independence with practical tools to transform their personal financial habits and drive real community impact. The program includes online courses covering: – Project Management (by Global Changemakers) – Understanding Misinformation (by Univision) – Financial Education (by Wells Fargo) Benefits While there is a $10 entry fee, participants who complete key milestones can earn incentives up to $205, receive specialized training, and become eligible to apply for $1,000 micro-grants to implement community projects. $205 in direct cash incentives, with milestone payments deposited directly into their savings account as you build healthy financial habits. Access to project management training and certification through Global Changemakers’ digital platform, helping you develop practical, workforce-ready skills. Eligible to compete for $1,000 project grants to launch a community impact initiative and join the Global Changemakers Network. 100% accessible — no college degree, previous journalism experience, or professional equipment is required. All you need is commitment and a smartphone. Eligibility This program is available for young people in the United States who are between 18-24 years old. The program is designed for beginners who want to build practical money habits and learn basic mobile storytelling. Current or prior college enrollment is not required. Requirements Personal Savings Account Verification: Submit documents of a valid savings account held in your name at a bank offering Zelle. Wells Fargo is recommended due to its low maintenance requirements. $15 Incentive. Educational Modules & Social Media Submissions: Complete all financial education playbooks on the Wells Fargo Saving Cents Platform & publish 3 educational videos on social media reflecting your financial learnings. Use tags #MoneyMovesChallenge #MediaImpactAcademy #GlobalChangemakers $90 Incentive Demonstration of Sustained Savings: Fill out the Completion Survey between March 28th – April 02 & provide documentation proving that the initial $50 received from prior incentives was retained in your account. $100 Incentive. Application Enroll in the program through the Global Changemakers platform. Complete coursework on Project Management. Complete the financial education playbooks from Wells Fargo. Once you have completed both educational components, you can apply to get your Community Action Project to become a reality. Submit your application to Global Changemakers and start creating a positive impact in your community. Click here to apply . For more information, visit Global Changemakers . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Spencer Fellowship for Education Reporting 2027 (Funded) Next Article Call for judges : Join the OD Impact Challenge 2026 global judging panel Opportunity Desk Website Opportunity Desk is the one stop place for all global opportunities. Connect with us on Facebook, Twitter and Instagram - @opportunitydesk Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 November 10, 2026 Closes in 24 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter