n Ukraine so far this year, up from nine over the previous two years. Ukraine’s defense intelligence agency, the GUR, reported last week that a former taxi driver from Indonesia’s capital, Jakarta, Taufiq Muhammad, had been killed in Ukraine after signing a one-year contract to serve in the Russian military. “Taufiq died almost immediately, during his very first battle,” the GUR wrote. Mewengkang said Indonesia was still seeking to verify Taufiq’s death. Indonesian officials have previously raised the alarm about what they say are deceptive practices used to lure Indonesians to the war’s front lines. Government officials are still trying to verify the whereabouts of eight Indonesian citizens who ended up in the Russian military in 2025 after reportedly traveling for civilian jobs in security and administration. The country’s director-general of immigration, Hendarsam Marantoko, said last month that Indonesians were often lured by the prospect of non-military work. \"When they went there, the offer wasn't to join the military, that was the problem. Once they arrived, they had a hard time returning home,” he was quoted as saying by Antara. The Russian Embassy in Jakarta did not respond to a request for comment. November 2, 2026 Share Article: Reported by Tom Allard OCCRP Related Articles 3 weeks ago Russia Detains Japanese Journalist on Espionage Charges Freedom and Repression Russia 3 months ago Russia Charges Telegram Founder Durov With Aiding Terrorism Freedom and Repression Russia 3 months ago Russian Security Service Planned AI Tool to Track Media Freedom and Repression Russia 3 weeks ago Russia Detains Japanese Journalist on Espionage Charges Freedom and Repression Russia 3 months ago Russia Charges Telegram Founder Durov With Aiding Terrorism Freedom and Repression Russia 3 months ago Russian Security Service Planned AI Tool to Track Media Freedom and Repression Russia Help us improve the website! Click below to give us input. It’ll only take 5 minutes. 👉 Help 