        "evidenceText": "Seven Arrested in International Operation Targeting Investment Fraud | OCCRP Organized Crime • Europe Seven Arrested in International Operation Targeting Investment Fraud November 3, 2026 | 1 min read Share Article &times; Aa Text Settings &times; Text Size Small Medium Large Line Spacing Compact Normal Spacious Authorities from seven countries seized more than 100 servers and arrested seven people suspected of being involved in an alleged investment fraud that may have cost victims in at least 50 countries more than $4.6 million. Tuesday’s operation, led by German prosecutors and supported by Europol and Eurojust, targeted a company that operated in Cyprus and Israel and supplied platforms to criminal groups running call centers in Albania, Kosovo and North Macedonia. The scheme relied on misleading online advertisements promising high returns from cryptocurrency, foreign exchange, and stock trading. Victims were encouraged to make larger deposits after their accounts showed fictitious profits, but then withdrawals were subsequently blocked. The investigation began in 2022 after a German couple reported being unable to recover their investments. November 3, 2026 Share Article: Related Articles 6 hours ago Interpol Crackdown on Migrant Smuggling Nets 262 Arrests Organized Crime Africa 2 weeks ago Smugglers Collected Up to $509M on Europe Routes in 2025 Organized Crime Europe 1 month ago Kidnappings and Home Invasions Soar as French Syndicates Extort Crypto Organized Crime Europe 6 hours ago Interpol Crackdown on Migrant Smuggling Nets 262 Arrests Organized Crime Africa 2 weeks ago Smugglers Collected Up to $509M on Europe Routes in 2025 Organized Crime Europe 1 month ago Kidnappings and Home Invasions Soar as French Syndicates Extort Crypto Organized Crime Europe Help us improve the website! Click below to give us input. It’ll only take 5 minutes. 👉 Help OCCRP Don't show this anymore",
